          <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1598256989800-fe5f95da9787?w=800&q=80" alt="Ceramic Crown treatment at Dr. Ravi's Clinic" loading="lazy">
        </div>
        <div class="service-detail-content">
          <p>A ceramic crown is a tooth-shaped cap that completely covers a damaged tooth to restore its shape, size, strength, and appearance. At our clinic, we use high-grade zirconia, porcelain, and E-max ceramics that mimic the translucency and color of natural enamel.</p><h3>When Do You Need a Crown?</h3><ul><li>After root canal treatment to protect the weakened tooth</li><li>To restore a severely worn down or broken tooth</li><li>To cover a dental implant</li><li>To hold a dental bridge in place</li><li>To cover misshapen or severely discolored teeth</li><li>For cosmetic smile makeovers</li></ul><h3>Types of Crowns We Offer</h3><p><strong>Zirconia Crowns:</strong> Extremely durable, biocompatible, and ideal for posterior teeth. They resist chipping and wear.</p><p><strong>Porcelain-Fused-to-Metal (PFM):</strong> Strong metal core with porcelain coating. Good balance of strength and aesthetics.</p><p><strong>E-Max (Lithium Disilicate):</strong> Premium all-ceramic crowns with exceptional aesthetics for front teeth.</p><h3>The Crown Procedure</h3><p>We prepare the tooth, take digital impressions, place a temporary crown, and fabricate your permanent crown in our partner lab. The final crown is cemented in place at your second visit — typically within 5-7 days.</p>
          <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
          <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
            <div class="faq-item"><button type="button" class="faq-question">How long do ceramic crowns last? <span class="faq-icon"><i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i></span></button><div class="faq-answer"><p>With proper care, ceramic crowns last 10-15 years or longer. Avoid biting ice, hard candy, and grinding.</p></div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><button type="button" class="faq-question">Do crowns look natural? <span class="faq-icon"><i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i></span></button><div class="faq-answer"><p>Absolutely. We shade-match every crown to your surrounding teeth for seamless integration.</p></div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><button type="button" class="faq-question">Is the crown procedure painful? <span class="faq-icon"><i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i></span></button><div class="faq-answer"><p>The tooth is numbed with local anesthesia. You may feel mild sensitivity for a few days after preparation.</p></div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
